Bare-metal S-Boot payload probes for the Galaxy A3 2017 (no UART needed).

  rebootdl.S     paints the framebuffer red, then reboots into download mode via PMU
                 INFORM3/SWRESET. If the phone returns to download mode by itself, S-Boot
                 ran our code.
  decon_probe.c  tests DECON trigger modes on the command-mode panel (see CLAUDE.md, Display).
  asv-fuse/      kernel module (not a payload): reads the secure-only ASV fuses at 0x100d9000 through
                 the vendor SMC, prints them, then refuses to load. Build with the kernel's Kbuild
                 (make ARCH=arm64 -C <kernel out dir> M=$PWD/asv-fuse) and insmod on the phone.
                 Superseded in practice by exynos7870-asv, which logs the group at boot.
  ssp-probe.c    userspace sensor hub probe (phone, Linux): WHOAMI, FIRMWARE_REV and
                 SENSOR_SCANNING over spidev + GPIO chardev, read commands only; never touches the
                 MCU reset or BOOT0 lines. Build with ./ssp-probe-build (needs the kernel uapi
                 headers: make ... headers), dry run on the host: qemu-aarch64-static ./ssp-probe -n.
                 On the phone: bind spidev to spi4.0 (driver_override) with the sensorhub module
                 not loaded, then ./ssp-probe. See work/notes/sensorhub.md section 7.
  ssp-pins.sh    read-only state of the sensor hub pins (function, level, pull) via peek.

Build (from this directory):
  aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc -nostdlib -nostartfiles -Wl,-Ttext=0 -Wl,--build-id=none -o rebootdl.elf rebootdl.S
  aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc -O2 -ffreestanding -nostdlib -nostartfiles -fno-pic -fno-stack-protector \
    -mgeneral-regs-only -mstrict-align -mbranch-protection=none -Wl,-T,probe.lds -Wl,--build-id=none \
    -o decon_probe.elf decon_start.S decon_probe.c
  aarch64-linux-gnu-objcopy -O binary X.elf X.bin
Pack: mkbootimg-samsung --kernel X.bin --dt <dt.img> -o X.img ; flash to BOOT with a3-flash.
Check `xxd -l 64 X.bin` starts with the branch + text_offset 0x80000 + "ARMd" at 0x38.
